## Reviewer got wrong (not applied as suggested)

- b#1 suggested «به‌سبب باقی‌نماندن تصویر». That is the opposite of the English: the court does not draw an adverse inference merely because the footage no longer exists. The double negative in the old Persian was real; the fix uses «نبودن تصویر».
- a#14’s “(۲۰۲۰)” and any other Gregorian beside a Minguo year. R13 forbids a new digit. The calendar was renamed گاه‌شماری مینگو instead.
- a#3’s «۱٫۵۷ میلیون دلار جدید تایوان» for the pinned bio figure “TWD 1.57M”.
- b#11’s word “نیم” for 0.5, and the request to abandon comma thousands. R14 and the checker require “0.5” and “500,000” for fa. Part a already says business Persian accepts that grouping.
- a#12 and b#18, insofar as they ask to delete U+200B lines or to turn Q16–Q20 into new headings. Those lines match the Korean source the checker diffs against. The blog cadence is real; the structure is not free to change.
- a#24’s “delete this row” and b#19’s “delete this sentence”, insofar as each is its own table row or block. The cells and the sentence were rephrased in place.
